pendell@hotmail.com wrote:
> My list:
>
> Early game (pre-Sokoban):
> 1) Soldier ant.
> 2) Killer bee.

I'd put both of those in the mid-game, I usually don't see them before
Sokoban.  But yeah, they're nasty (esp. if you don't have poison
resistance yet).  Leocratta come to mind in the mid-game too.

DL1, foxes are probably the biggest threats.  But in the early game not
much stands out on it's own, everything _could_ kill you but nothing is
especially more likely than anything else (except floating eyes, which
are completely avoidable, and suicides like water demons/moccasins,
etc).

> Mid-game (Sokoban to castle):
> 1)  Mind flayer/master mind flayer.
> Reason:  Fast, magic-resistant,  flies,  many attacks per turn

Mind flayers are quite slow.  THROW ROCKS AT IT!  They're nasty if they
get summoned next to you, or if they appear way out-of-depth, but
generally by the time they appear you can take them down safely at
range and feast.  Even if they're summoned, they respect E.

Titan at Medusa is usually the toughest creature in this range (unless
you're a monk doing the quest), followed by liches at the castle if
they are spellcasters.

Golden Nagas can suck.

Mumaks can be problematic if you don't see them coming, they can take
you down in a hurry.

> 2) Black Dragon
> Reason: Disintegration instakill.  Lethal if one doesn't have
> reflection.

Sure, though I think I've only once run into one w/o reflection
(couldn't find reflection above the castle) and that was in the castle
where I was able to maneuver so it never used its breath weapon.

Gnome with a wand of death is a more common instakill, IMO.

> 3) Cockatrice
> Reason:  More ways to kill oneself with a cockatrice corpse than with

Yeah, only if you act foolishly.  If you're going to list this, then
I'd list floating eyes in the early game (and they're probably far
deadlier).

> Late game:
>
> 1) Arch-lich.
> Reason: Touch of death, teleportation,  destroy armor, summon monsters.

Dangerous, but I find Archons and Titans both much worse.

Of course, in the late game high priests, Rodney, Demogorgon, etc are
there.



